      "quality": "good"
    },
    {
      "id": 3,
      "text": "SR 230 and SR 231 run concurrently on Orange Road to the center of Pratts, where SR 231 turns south onto Blue Ridge Turnpike.",
      "sourceSentenceIds": [
        11
      ],
      "sourceLabels": [
        "Wikipedia"
      ],
      "source": "https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Virginia_State_Route_230",
      "category": "transport",
      "quality": "poor",
      "qualityReason": "route_only"
    },
    {
      "id": 4,
      "text": "A VDOT project plans a roundabout at the Routes 230/231 intersection to improve safety, with a public hearing in August 2025.",
      "sourceSentenceIds": [
        14
      ],
      "sourceLabels": [
        "Web source 1"
      ],
      "source": "https://grokipedia.com/page/pratts_virginia",
      "category": "other",
      "quality": "poor",
      "qualityReason": "other"
    },
    {
      "id": 5,
      "text": "Pratts lies about 2.4 miles southwest of Madison and 90 miles southwest of Washington, D.C., placing it in a rural setting near the Blue Ridge Mountains.",
      "sourceSentenceIds": [
        20
      ],
      "sourceLabels": [
        "Web source 1"
      ],
      "source": "https://grokipedia.com/page/pratts_virginia",
      "category": "other",
      "quality": "poor",
      "qualityReason": "location_description"
    },
    {
      "id": 6,
      "text": "The climate is humid subtropical, with warm humid summers averaging 85°F in July and cold winters averaging 23°F in January, sometimes snowing due to nearby Blue Ridge.",
